                <pb facs="0726" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.6363/29: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commissioner in Albania</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Blake</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-28T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>10. Sinclair Exploration Company reports that they are being severely handicapped
                    in effort to obtain oil concession by the activities of the Shell and
                    Anglo–Persian Oil Companies.</p>
                <p>Telegraph briefly exact status of negotiations of these foreign interests. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
